* >Natural Source Header 000000
* :Mode S
* :CP
* <Natural Source Header
*
* Sample program to call the "Reload Services" function
* on Natural OpenAPI Server via Natural Request Document
*
* !!! If this FAILS with NAT8304 and you are using HTTPS with a self-signed certificate !!! :
* Try on bash: curl -X POST https://city311linux.eur.ad.sag:9000/actuator/reloadServices
* Import trusted CA certificates into $SSL_CERT_FILE (/opt/softwareag/common/security/openssl/cert.pem)
* > cat "/opt/data/ssl/Software AG CA 2.crt" > $SSL_CERT_FILE
* > cat "/opt/data/ssl/Software AG Root CA 2020.crt" > $SSL_CERT_FILE
*
DEFINE DATA
LOCAL
1 #URL       (A) DYNAMIC
1 #HEADER    (A) DYNAMIC
1 #PAGE      (A) DYNAMIC
1 #RESULT    (A) DYNAMIC
1 #RC      (I4)
END-DEFINE
* Adapt the url to match your NOA Server Name and Management Port
ASSIGN #URL = 'https://city311linux.eur.ad.sag:9000/actuator/reloadServices'
*
REQUEST DOCUMENT FROM #URL
   WITH
     HEADER 'REQUEST-METHOD' VALUE 'POST'
            'Accept'   VALUE '*/*'
   RETURN
     PAGE #RESULT
RESPONSE #RC

PRINT '=' #RC / '=' #RESULT
END
